From: EiraOS Maintainers <maintainers@eira-os.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Add <core><trustedGroup>: stack and focus a trusted client's windows

A window of a client whose effective GID at connect() (SO_PEERCRED) is the
configured group lies above every other window, layer, popup, menu and drag
icon; only a session lock is above it. While it is mapped it has keyboard
focus; other windows cannot be focused, raised or activated, drags cannot
start, input grabs are ended, other clients cannot set a cursor image, and
it cannot be minimized. A group that does not exist or that labwc runs in
trusts nobody (fail closed).

Use case: a consent dialog installed setgid to a group with no members, so
an ordinary program running as the user can neither impersonate it nor
cover it (clickjacking). EiraOS: EIRA-CONSENT-AGENT R-6.2.

Applies to labwc 0.20.3 (e0a3970b0c70e321814e8004ff7c6dbc7aeaf884).
Tested by packaging/eira-labwc/verify-trusted.sh (headless, with control
runs). To be proposed upstream (UDVIKLINGSPLAN F0.1).
---
