+  <trustedGroup></trustedGroup>
   <promptCommand>[see details below]</promptCommand>
   <errorCommand>[see details below]</errorCommand>
 </core>
@@ -268,6 +269,22 @@ this is for compatibility with Openbox.
 	up/down) in Chromium and electron based clients without inadvertently
 	pasting the primary clipboard. Default is yes.
 
+*<core><trustedGroup>* [group name]
+	Windows of clients whose effective group ID at connect() is this group
+	(SO_PEERCRED) are stacked above all other windows, layer-shell
+	surfaces, popups, menus and drag icons; only a session lock is above
+	them. While such a window is mapped, it has keyboard focus, other
+	windows cannot be focused, raised or activated, drags cannot start,
+	input grabs are ended, other clients cannot set a cursor image, and
+	the window cannot be minimized.
+
+	Meant for a consent or authorization dialog installed setgid to a
+	group with no members, so that no other program can run with the group
+	(a process cannot gain an effective group it is not in). If the group
+	does not exist, or labwc itself runs in it, no window is trusted and an
+	error is logged. Combine with an empty *<privilegedInterfaces>* block,
+	or a client could still read or synthesize input. Default is unset.
+
 *<core><promptCommand>*
 	Set command to be invoked for an action prompt (*<action><prompt>*)
 
